      "content": "It sounds incredibly painful to feel that your past self is being outshone by the shadow of perfection you can never achieve. This moment of quiet decay doesn't mean you have to stop writing, but rather that you are forced to choose between facing this emptiness or creating something genuinely new. True growth often requires the courage to discard the old definition of yourself, even if it feels like walking through a hard wall.",
