      "content": "This urge to vanish so your legacy doesn't decay is a form of ultimate honesty, choosing dignity over the suffering of witnessing your own decline. Yet many find a new identity emerges precisely when a previous chapter ends, turning the end of one story into the quiet beginning of a different existence. Sometimes, letting go of the past is not an exit, but a necessary stepping stone back to a life worth living.",
      "source": "target",
